.TH JETHROD 1 "2026-11-13" "jethrod 0.2.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jethrod \- daemon that listens for Jethro Tull / Ian Anderson North American tour dates
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jethrod
.RB [ \-c
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-state\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-pidfile
.IR file ]
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B jethrod run
.RB [ \-d | \-\-daemon ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-\-log
.RI [ file ]]
.RB [ \-\-syslog ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B jethrod
polls the official tour feed behind jethrotull.com/tour\-dates (default every
30 minutes) and raises a high\-priority alert the first time a date in the
United States, Canada or Mexico appears. Once a day (default 08:00 local) it
also compares every news post, page, discography, video, gallery, merch and
band entry on jethrotull.com against what it saw last time and sends one
low\-priority digest of anything new or changed.
.PP
Alerts go to the desktop (terminal\-notifier or osascript on macOS, a toast on
Windows, notify\-send on Linux) and, if configured, to a phone through
.BR ntfy .
Every item alerts exactly once; a delivery that fails on every channel is
retried on the next poll.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the daemon. Stays in the foreground (what systemd, launchd and OpenRC
expect) unless
.B \-\-daemon
is given.
.TP
.BR stop ", " reload ", " kick " [" \-\-site ]
Signal the running daemon (found via its pidfile): SIGTERM, SIGHUP, SIGUSR1 or
SIGUSR2. Exit status 3 if it is not running.
.TP
.B install\-service
Linux: write and enable a systemd \-\-user unit. Windows: add a Startup
shortcut and start now. macOS: use
.BR "brew services start jethrod" .
.TP
.B uninstall\-service
Undo
.BR install\-service .
.TP
.B check
Check the tour feed once. Exit 2 if something new was found.
.TP
.BR site " [" \-\-recent ]
Run the site digest once, or list the 10 most recently changed items.
.TP
.B status
Daemon state, paths, alert history and every booked date
.RB ( >>
marks North American ones). Exit 3 if the daemon is not running.
.TP
.BR test\-alert ", " selftest ", " forget
Send a test on every channel; verify the geography logic; clear all history.
.TP
.BR config " [" \fIkey\fR " " \fIvalue\fR ]
Show the effective configuration, or set one key in the user config file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIfile\fR"
Configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " dir"
Where seen.json (and by default the pidfile and log) live.
.TP
.BI \-\-pidfile " file"
Pidfile. It is also an exclusive lock: a second daemon exits 1, and a stale
file left by a crash never blocks a start.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Double\-fork, setsid, chdir /, umask 022, stdio to /dev/null. For sysvinit.
Implies
.B \-\-log
unless
.B \-\-syslog
is given.
.TP
.BR \-\-log " [\fIfile\fR]"
Log to a file (default
.IR <state\-dir>/jethrod.log ).
The file is reopened automatically after rotation.
.TP
.B \-\-syslog
Log to syslog, facility daemon.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Debug logging.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Finish the current step, remove the pidfile, exit 0.
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Re\-read the configuration and reopen the log.
.TP
.B SIGUSR1
Check the tour feed now.
.TP
.B SIGUSR2
Run the site digest now.
.SH SYSTEMD
.B jethrod
is a
.B Type=notify
service: it sends READY=1, STATUS=, RELOADING=1, STOPPING=1 and, when
.B WatchdogSec=
is set, WATCHDOG=1 keep\-alives, without needing libsystemd. Under the journal
it logs with
.BR sd\-daemon (3)
priority prefixes. It honours
.BR $STATE_DIRECTORY ,
.BR $CONFIGURATION_DIRECTORY ,
.B $RUNTIME_DIRECTORY
and
.BR $LOGS_DIRECTORY .
.SH CONFIGURATION
A plain
.I key=value
file;
.B #
starts a comment. Keys:
.B interval_minutes
(30, minimum 5),
.B ntfy_topic
(empty = off),
.B ntfy_server
(https://ntfy.sh),
.B desktop
(on|off),
.B site_watch
(on|off),
.B digest_time
(HH:MM local, 08:00),
.BR feed ,
.B site
(https://jethrotull.com).
Each key can be overridden by an environment variable
.BR JETHROD_ \fIKEY\fR,
e.g.
.BR JETHROD_NTFY_TOPIC .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/jethrod/config
System\-wide configuration (POSIX), read first.
.TP
.IR ~/.config/jethrod/config ", " %APPDATA%\ejethrod\econfig
Per\-user configuration (root uses /etc/jethrod/config).
.TP
.IR ~/.local/state/jethrod/ ", " /var/lib/jethrod/ ", " %LOCALAPPDATA%\ejethrod\e
State:
.I seen.json
(what has been alerted, the site baseline), default pidfile and log.
.TP
.I contrib/
systemd system and user units, sysvinit and OpenRC scripts, logrotate config
(installed under
.I $(brew \-\-prefix)/share/jethrod/contrib
by Homebrew).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR JETHROD_CONFIG ", " JETHROD_STATE_DIR ", " JETHROD_PIDFILE ,
.BR JETHROD_ \fIKEY\fR,
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME ,
.BR NOTIFY_SOCKET ", " WATCHDOG_USEC ", " JOURNAL_STREAM .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error, or another daemon already holds the pidfile.
.TP
.B 2
.B check
found new North American dates; or a usage error.
.TP
.B 3
.BR stop ", " reload ", " kick ", " status :
the daemon is not running (LSB).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
jethrod config ntfy_topic jethrod\-$(openssl rand \-hex 6)
jethrod test\-alert
jethrod install\-service
journalctl \-\-user \-u jethrod \-f
jethrod kick \-\-site
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR sd_notify (3),
.BR start\-stop\-daemon (8),
.BR openrc\-run (8),
.BR logrotate (8),
https://ntfy.sh,
https://jethrotull.com/tour\-dates/
.SH NOTES
Unofficial fan toy; not affiliated with Jethro Tull or Ian Anderson.
